1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,575
Sound does not fade. It jumps.

2
00:00:05,575 --> 00:00:11,945
Sound is vibration. Vibration is energy.

3
00:00:11,945 --> 00:00:19,113
That energy comes in packets called phonons

4
00:00:19,113 --> 00:00:27,076
Energy sits on steps. Nothing in between.

5
00:00:27,076 --> 00:00:34,244
Watched single phonons jump between steps, in real time

6
00:00:34,244 --> 00:00:40,615
A resonator that rings for about 2 milliseconds

7
00:00:40,615 --> 00:00:46,985
The first direct real-time observation of a phonon jump

8
00:00:46,985 --> 00:00:52,560
Ions in 1986. Photons in 2007. Sound in 2026.
